Chapter: BoundedSigStatic

 Bounded signatures, stage A (BoundedSignatures.md): the function
 boundary draws the same hybrid narrowing check as a record field. A
 literal argument proven within a bounded parameter reports CDX2053
 (bounds check elided), and an argument proven in range by the
 interval analysis (an if-union) also elides. The unproven
 body-into-bounded-return shape is rejected since CDX2051 became an
 error; its twin lives in errors/narrowing-unproven. The sidecars pin
 the proven diagnostic and the in-range behavior.

Section: Definitions

  inc-byte : Integer between 0 and 255 -> Integer
  inc-byte (n) = n + 1

  clamp-level : Integer between 0 and 15 -> Integer
  clamp-level (n) = n + 1

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
   print-line-uni (integer-to-text (inc-byte 5))
   print-line-uni (integer-to-text (clamp-level (if True then 3 else 12)))
  end
